1. Credit Text

Every Derivative Deliverable must include the following credit text,
verbatim and in full. A translation into another language is permitted
only if the names and both links are reproduced exactly and unchanged:

    Built on the open-source ShopWise project — Copyright (c) 2026 Muhammed Bekiroğlu and the ShopWise contributors.

    Original ShopWise repository: https://github.com/Mohamad1234567891/ShopWise

    Muhammed Bekiroğlu (ShopWise team leader and top contributor) YouTube channel: https://www.youtube.com/@ALShajaraComputerScienceInstit

2. Where the Credit Text Must Appear

2.1 Documentation. The credit text must appear in every README file,
    documentation file, or other explanatory file distributed with the
    Derivative Deliverable (for example, README files, documentation
    pages, user manuals, and other files whose purpose is to explain the
    software). Including the credit text only in a license file does not
    satisfy this requirement.

2.2 User Interface. The credit text must also be visible to end users of
    the Derivative Deliverable, as follows:

    (a) If the Derivative Deliverable has a graphical user interface, the
        credit text must be accessible from that interface through a
        clearly named credits, attribution, or about screen, dialog,
        button, menu entry, or equivalent means. If the Derivative
        Deliverable displays its own credits or third-party credits, the
        ShopWise credit text must be included together with them, and may
        not be omitted in favor of, or hidden behind, those credits.

    (b) If the Derivative Deliverable is a command-line application, the
        credit text must be printed in the terminal at the beginning of
        every run of the application.

    (c) If the Derivative Deliverable provides both a graphical user
        interface and a command-line interface, paragraphs (a) and (b)
        both apply: the credit text must be accessible from the graphical
        interface as described in paragraph (a), and it must also be
        printed in the terminal at the beginning of every run as
        described in paragraph (b). Satisfying only one of the two is not
        sufficient.

    (d) The credit text need not appear on every screen, window, or page;
        one clearly accessible location in each interface that satisfies
        the applicable paragraph above is sufficient.

2.3 Clickable Links. Wherever the credit text is displayed in electronic
    form — in a graphical interface, in terminal output, or in an
    electronic document — the Original ShopWise repository link and the
    YouTube channel link must be clickable hyperlinks, or otherwise
    directly actionable links, leading to the exact addresses shown in
    Section 1. Rendering the links as plain, non-clickable text is not
    sufficient in any medium that supports clickable links.

3. Credits in the ShopWise Source Files

Every Python source file of the original ShopWise project carries a file
header at the top, identifying ShopWise, the copyright holders, the
Original ShopWise repository, the YouTube channel of the team leader,
and the license under which the file is distributed. No person may
remove, alter, shorten, or obscure those headers, and no person may
replace them with their own credits, except as follows:

3.1 If a ShopWise source file is distributed unmodified, its original
    file header must remain exactly as it is, and no credits of any
    other person may be added to that file.

3.2 If a ShopWise source file has been modified, the person who modified
    it may add their own credits to that file, but only if:

    (a) the original ShopWise file header remains intact and unchanged;
        and

    (b) the file clearly states that it is a modified version of the
        original ShopWise file.

